From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 17:37:54 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 05/35] fix(refinery): resolve the merge approval gate from the
 formula's own pack tree (gcp-amo)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Turning require_merge_approval on did not gate merges — it hard-stopped the
refinery on every patrol iteration. The four-candidate lookup the gate shipped
with could not resolve merge-approval-gate.sh from the context the formula
actually runs in, so patrol printed "An unreadable gate is not an approval",
drain-acked, and exited 1 before touching any bead. Fail-closed became
fail-forever.

Every candidate was unreachable by construction, not by accident. GC_PACK_DIR
is exported only when gc invokes a *pack command*; a formula's inline bash is
the agent's own shell, and the var is unset in every running agent process in
the city. Nothing materializes pack check scripts into $GC_CITY/.gc/scripts/
checks/, so candidates 2-4 pointed at a directory that has never existed. This
was the only formula-invoked check using that lookup pattern — the sibling
check scripts are reached as pack commands, where GC_PACK_DIR *is* set — so the
strategy had no working precedent anywhere and was never exercised end to end.

The gate now resolves primarily from this formula's own source path, reported
by `gc formula list --json`: the gate ships beside the formula in the same pack
tree, so that anchor is present whenever the formula is, needs no environment
beyond the city, and is version-coherent by construction — a formula from one
pin can never reach a gate from another. It works identically for a rig pinned
to a SHA, because gc checks the pin out into the content-addressed pack cache
and reports that path. GC_PACK_DIR and the city scripts dir stay as fallbacks
for cities that stage checks themselves; an unresolvable gate still refuses to
merge, unchanged.

Chose formula-side resolution over the two alternatives deliberately. Having gc
materialize pack checks into the city scripts dir, or export GC_PACK_DIR into
agent sessions, would both need gc-binary changes plus new deploy machinery,
and neither gives the version coherence that anchoring on the formula's own
tree does for free.

Validation: the wiring block is delimited by markers and the tests execute it
verbatim rather than a transcription, so the resolution strategy cannot regress
silently. New coverage asserts resolution with GC_PACK_DIR unset (the real
runtime condition), resolution from a SHA-pinned pack cache path, the city
scripts fallback, the fail-closed stop when nothing resolves, and — the
behaviour the bug denied — that a resolvable gate parks an unapproved bead as
merge_approval_state=awaiting_review instead of drain-acking. Verified red
against the pre-fix lookup in the same scenario, and confirmed live from the
refinery worktree with the real gc and GC_PACK_DIR unset that resolution lands
on the pinned pack cache tree.

Follow-up: tests/test_no_bare_bd_commands.py is already red on integration from
the gcp-dc8 stack — filed as gcp-1q4, discovered-from this bead. This change
adds no new violations to it.
